CLAUDE.md

# steph 16/09: the synthetic fixture is a dev/test tool (src/comparator/fixtures.py
# builds it in memory for the test suite). Committing a synthetic DATA file invites
# someone to run the analysis on it and read the result as a finding.
data/fixtures/

# web UI build artefacts
web/node_modules/
web/dist/

# steph 18/09: Dan's Google Trends benchmark is a separate project with its own
# source and data (app.py, collectors/, 141 CSVs). We consume its export/ folder
# at src/comparator/trends.py:DEFAULT_EXPORT_DIR, which already degrades to
# nothing when it is absent, so check it out rather than vendoring 7.7 MB of
# another repo's code and third-party data into this one. The derived
# web/public/trends.json is committed, so the UI works without it.
kbc-ing-benchmark/
